ICU's HIDDEN_OVERLAY check tests the identifier as written, while its INVISIBLE
check tests the NFD form. So U+0130 LATIN CAPITAL LETTER I WITH DOT ABOVE
passes but its canonical equivalent, I followed by U+0307 COMBINING DOT ABOVE,
fails (I's confusable prototype is l), and the NFC form of l, U+0323, U+0307
passes where the NFD form fails. Unicode conformance clause C6 asks processes
not to treat canonically equivalent strings as distinct, and NFC, the usual
form for stored identifiers, is the one that slips through. This patch tests
the NFD form, as confusable does. Drop it once ICU fixes this upstream.

--- a/source/i18n/uspoof.cpp
+++ b/source/i18n/uspoof.cpp
@@ -592,7 +592,11 @@
     }
 
     if (0 != (This->fChecks & USPOOF_HIDDEN_OVERLAY)) {
-        int32_t index = This->findHiddenOverlay(id, *status);
+        // Test the NFD form, as the INVISIBLE check does, so that canonically
+        // equivalent strings get the same result.
+        UnicodeString nfdId;
+        gNfdNormalizer->normalize(id, nfdId, *status);
+        int32_t index = This->findHiddenOverlay(nfdId, *status);
         if (index != -1) {
             result |= USPOOF_HIDDEN_OVERLAY;
         }
